# Code style

TypeScript only. Do not add `.js` or `.jsx` files.

Use arrow functions assigned to `const`. Do not use `function` declarations or `function` expressions. Give exported functions an explicit return type. Prefer `import type`, `satisfies`, `as const`, and unions over `enum` and `any`.

```ts
export const getExplorePercent = (index: number, count: number): number =>
  count <= 1 ? 0 : Math.round((index / (count - 1)) * 100);
```

Keep each concept in its own folder under `src/`:

- `components/` — markup and composition only
- `hooks/` — stateful React logic
- `helpers/` — pure functions
- `data/` — content and constants
- `styles/` — CSS
- `types/` — shared types
- `tests/` — unit tests only

A component imports those pieces. It does not declare data, shared types, or business logic inline.

Do not write an anonymous function at the call site. Name it with a `const` arrow and pass that name. This includes JSX handlers and array callbacks. Test-runner callbacks (`describe`, `it`) stay as the runner requires.

```tsx
const goHome = (): void => go("home");

<button type="button" onClick={goHome}>
  AN
</button>
```

Do not hardcode `px` or one-off sizes in a component. Declare the value once in `src/data/design.ts` and reuse the exported const or the CSS variable it injects.

Typography comes from `src/styles/system.css` (`type-display`, `type-title`, `type-heading`, `type-body`, `type-eyebrow`, `type-meta`, `type-nav`, `type-brand`). Use those classes. Do not repeat font size, line height, or letter spacing on a component.

Every exported helper and hook has a unit test under `src/tests/`, mirroring the source path: `src/helpers/scroll.ts` is tested by `src/tests/helpers/scroll.test.ts`. The test calls the function directly. Test a hook with `renderHook`. Do not add a test that only renders a component, and do not place test files next to source.
